/-!
# Root representatives for F4 Schreier reduction

The 48 states are reached from the eight signed simple roots by shortest
simple-reflection words. The initial states have empty representatives.
Kernel-checked integer-coordinate evaluations show that a representative can
end at a signed simple root only at its corresponding initial state.

The ordering and transition table are generated by `source/generate_certificates.py`.
The generator is not trusted: `routeCoeff_eq` and `route_terminal` check its
coordinate claims, while `Certificates.lean` checks every transition as an
identity in the actual Weyl group. Source: GLS3 Lemma 2.9.4.
-/

@[expose] public section

